# Inbox route — [item title]

> An inbox item is anything you've captured from outside the system. Use this template to route the item to its destination.

## 1. Source

Where did the item come from?

- **Channel:** [X, RSS, conversation, screenshot, book, podcast, etc.]
- **URL / reference:** [the canonical link or reference]
- **Author / origin:** [who or what produced the item]
- **Date captured:** [when you captured it]

## 2. Type

What kind of item is it?

- **Type:** [article, post, screenshot, idea, decision, conversation, voice-memo, etc.]
- **Length:** [short / medium / long]
- **Format:** [text / image / audio / video]

## 3. Action

What routing decision did you make?

- [ ] **Promote to atomic** (one idea per file, in your own words)
- [ ] **Promote to literature** (external source you're referencing)
- [ ] **File as skill-brief ticket** (recurring pattern, build a procedure)
- [ ] **File as strike-rule ticket** (failure pattern, observe 3+ times)
- [ ] **File as cron-spec ticket** (detection + surface + act pattern)
- [ ] **File as council ticket** (multi-perspective review needed)
- [ ] **File as operator-action ticket** (decision needs operator judgment)
- [ ] **Archive** (informational, no use case)
- [ ] **Delete** (noise, no value)

## 4. Notes

Why this routing? 1 sentence.

> [The 1-sentence reason this routing decision is correct]

The notes are **the audit trail.** When you look back at the inbox item 6 months later, the notes tell you why you made this decision.

---

## Approval

- [ ] Source is documented (channel, URL, author, date)
- [ ] Type is specific (article / post / etc.)
- [ ] Action is from the 9-action list
- [ ] Notes explain the routing
- [ ] Item is in the inbox tier (not in atomic / literature yet)
- [ ] Item is < 30 days old (if older, archive or re-evaluate)
- [ ] If the action is "File as operator-action ticket" or similar — the ticket is routed to the correct board via the keyword-routing table (see `methodology/04b-decide-board-routing.md`)

Once all 7 boxes are checked, the route is ready. Move the item to its destination tier.
